  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1148 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nMonday through Friday:\n\nHigh pressure will continue to linger over the northern Great\nLakes Monday ahead of an approaching cutoff low over Iowa.\nChances for scattered rain (15 to 30% PoPs) will persist through\nthe day as some moisture tries to work into the area from the\ncutoff low, but ultimately runs into the subsidence of the \nhigh. The cutoff low should lift back into the background zonal \nflow aloft Monday night into Tuesday and precip chances should \nlargely end by Tuesday morning. \n\nDry conditions then look to be in store for the rest of the\nextended period. Some residual troughing aloft will keep us cool\nthrough the mid week period with highs in the low to mid 60s.\n70s then return for the upcoming weekend as ridging begins to\nbuild over the upper MS Valley.\n\nCMiller",
